      "rationale": [
        "Read the complete canonical page and retained solution theorem, including its row convention and attribution scope. Both original bounds are retained with exactly distinct uniformity: the first constant precedes alpha,N,shifts; the second constant may depend on alpha only. The full numerator/denominator, real exponents, weak bounds and open parameter endpoints match.",
        "The Fin(2*N+1) reindexing uses signed subtraction after casting and covers all frequencies -N through N. Rows are nodes and columns frequencies. Exponentials of the real representatives give the original circle evaluations. The shift bound is weak and includes every endpoint and arbitrary sign pattern; no extra determinant premise restricts the target.",
        "The actual interpolant uses unnormalized W inverse; the normalized F inverse has precisely 1/sqrt(m) in F and is reserved for the Euclidean spectral norm. The joint complex polydisk/closed-interval supremum directly gives the original interpolation operator norm. Compactness, continuity and distinct nodes justify the ordinary supremum and genuine inverses without extra assumed premises.",
        "Both quantities remain separately defined and Target conjoins both bounds. There is no sampled interval, altered Fourier size, alpha=1/4 endpoint, log loss, finite N cutoff or norm conversion changing powers. No additional computation or analytic proof is needed merely to state these concrete propositions."
